1
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:13,750
Let's take the rear exit.

2
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:18,500
Shirou!

3
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:20,420
What is it, Saber?

4
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,130
I'm surprised to
see Saber with you.

5
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:29,760
You...

6
00:00:45,190 --> 00:00:50,230
In the face of absolute despair

7
00:00:50,530 --> 00:00:54,230
That nearly burned
our hearts away

8
00:00:55,730 --> 00:01:00,780
You still found the
courage to smile

9
00:01:01,030 --> 00:01:05,580
Like you accepted it all

10
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:08,840
I lost my voice

11
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:11,460
And the things I wanted to say

12
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:16,710
But every time I
fell to my knees

13
00:01:17,060 --> 00:01:21,010
I stood up and kept walking

14
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:26,680
We were looking for
the ideal white future

15
00:01:26,890 --> 00:01:31,910
Our one and only hope

16
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:34,400
Now I may be left with nothing

17
00:01:34,570 --> 00:01:39,820
But these raging
emotions that have

18
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:42,920
Nowhere to go

19
00:01:43,170 --> 00:01:48,170
Still, I'll look for a new dawn

20
00:01:48,550 --> 00:01:51,580
With more than one right answer

21
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:55,410
I won't stop

22
00:01:55,710 --> 00:01:57,440
Until I find it

23
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:09,240
Archer! What are you
doing showing up now?

24
00:02:09,241 --> 00:02:11,910
The Distance Between Them

25
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:13,279
Isn't it obvious? I sensed a threat
to my Master and rushed to her side.

26
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:15,580
But it appears I was too late.

27
00:02:15,910 --> 00:02:18,369
Yes, it's all over!

28
00:02:18,370 --> 00:02:20,320
I'll fill you in on
everything that happened

29
00:02:20,332 --> 00:02:22,249
while you were busy
taking your sweet time,

30
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:23,500
so stay put and listen!

31
00:02:24,670 --> 00:02:27,340
Looks like I arrived at
the worst possible time.

32
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:29,969
You can say that again!

33
00:02:29,970 --> 00:02:33,930
A Servant got eliminated,
and you show up after the fact?

34
00:02:34,470 --> 00:02:36,179
All right, all right.

35
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:38,100
Next time, I'll rush
to your side at once.

36
00:02:38,930 --> 00:02:42,270
So, which Servant
was eliminated?

37
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:48,240
It was Rider.

38
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:52,610
I don't know exactly what happened,
but she was probably taken out by Caster.

39
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:55,159
How spineless.

40
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:57,410
I suppose she
really was all talk.

41
00:02:57,790 --> 00:03:00,999
Archer, Rider died
protecting her Master.

42
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,249
You are in no position
to call her spineless.

43
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:05,289
She was spineless all the same.

44
00:03:05,290 --> 00:03:07,387
One who calls herself
a hero should at

45
00:03:07,399 --> 00:03:09,840
least try to take her
opponent out with her.

46
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:14,889
That she went down without a fight
suggests she was unable to do so.

47
00:03:14,890 --> 00:03:18,890
You insult the manner of her
death, and you call yourself a hero?

48
00:03:19,470 --> 00:03:22,196
Well, hero or not, it stands
to reason that anyone who

49
00:03:22,208 --> 00:03:25,149
isn't worthy of this battle
should be eliminated early on.

50
00:03:25,150 --> 00:03:26,609
Well said.

51
00:03:26,610 --> 00:03:28,610
In that case, do you
wish to fight me, Archer?

52
00:03:29,990 --> 00:03:34,449
I am compelled by a
Command Spell not to do so.

53
00:03:34,450 --> 00:03:38,949
And without the ability to fight
back, I would die just like Rider.

54
00:03:38,950 --> 00:03:41,790
Is that in keeping with
your code of chivalry, Saber?

55
00:03:43,870 --> 00:03:45,629
Archer, that's enough.

56
00:03:45,630 --> 00:03:51,089
My alliance with Emiya-kun lasts until
we defeat the Master hiding at school.

57
00:03:51,090 --> 00:03:55,139
Or what? Do you want to force me to
use another Command Spell on you?

58
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:56,849
Fair enough.

59
00:03:56,850 --> 00:04:01,849
Saber is so noble and righteous
that I got carried away teasing her.

60
00:04:01,850 --> 00:04:03,639
My apologies, Saber.

61
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:07,479
No, my behavior
was immature as well.

62
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:10,610
Out of respect for Rin, I
shall overlook your words.

63
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:14,729
Anyway, if we're going
to defeat Caster, the

64
00:04:14,741 --> 00:04:17,199
first thing we need to
do is locate her Master.

65
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:22,039
And for better or worse, they
come to this school every day.

66
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:27,079
Rather than spooking them and putting
them on guard, we should let them be.

67
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:28,080
In other words,

68
00:04:28,081 --> 00:04:32,919
after we identify the Master, we attack
before they can return to Ryuudou Temple?

69
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:34,169
Exactly.

70
00:04:34,170 --> 00:04:36,945
But after a big ruckus
like this, won't they

71
00:04:36,957 --> 00:04:39,680
deem it too risky to
keep attending school?

72
00:04:39,930 --> 00:04:41,719
That's unlikely.

73
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:45,189
I doubt Caster's Master still
possesses a will of their own.

74
00:04:45,190 --> 00:04:46,809
Knowing her,

75
00:04:46,810 --> 00:04:50,440
her very first move was probably
to turn her Master into a puppet.

76
00:04:51,690 --> 00:04:53,030
That makes sense.

77
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:57,819
Anyway, we'll continue our
investigation of the school.

78
00:04:57,820 --> 00:05:01,119
When we locate
Caster's Master, we strike.

79
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:05,289
That sounds reasonable,
but how do we look for them?

80
00:05:05,290 --> 00:05:07,459
That'll be our
homework for next time.

81
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:09,079
We're all tired.

82
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,539
Let's call it a day.

83
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:12,340
No, I can still...

84
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:19,049
Hey... Tohsaka!

85
00:05:19,050 --> 00:05:22,139
Can't you see that
Archer's acting strangely?

86
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:23,719
Don't you remember
what happened yesterday?

87
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,679
We need to wrap this up now!

88
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:27,599
Okay, I get it! I'll go home.

89
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:29,000
I won't press the
point any longer.

90
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:31,519
See you tomorrow, then.

91
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:33,939
Oh, and good work today.

92
00:05:33,940 --> 00:05:38,110
I could actually see you as
a Master, even if only a little.

93
00:05:38,990 --> 00:05:40,489
Let's go, Archer!

94
00:05:40,490 --> 00:05:43,620
I'll give you a proper
talking-to when we get back!

95
00:05:44,490 --> 00:05:46,619
Ah, there it is.

96
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:49,619
The uncharacteristic lack of
verbal abuse was troubling me.

97
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:54,960
Now, look here. Do I
need to lay down the law?

98
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:01,969
You want to sleep in my room?

99
00:06:01,970 --> 00:06:03,809
Of course.

100
00:06:03,810 --> 00:06:06,679
To prevent last night's
disaster from reoccurring,

101
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,849
I will be sleeping in your room.

102
00:06:08,850 --> 00:06:10,399
I trust you have no objections.

103
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:12,729
I do! Big ones!

104
00:06:12,730 --> 00:06:14,069
When it comes down to it,

105
00:06:14,070 --> 00:06:18,279
this is your fault for falling victim to
remote hypnosis from such a great distance.

106
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:22,659
I cannot protect you
from Caster's magic,

107
00:06:22,660 --> 00:06:25,329
so the least I can do is stay
as close to you as possible.

108
00:06:25,330 --> 00:06:28,749
Well, that is pretty
reasonable, but...

109
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:30,370
Look, tonight...

110
00:06:31,670 --> 00:06:33,249
All right.

111
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:35,880
You can sleep nearby.

112
00:06:36,170 --> 00:06:39,380
Good. That is the logical
course of action for a Master.

113
00:06:40,090 --> 00:06:42,680
But only nearby.

114
00:06:58,490 --> 00:07:02,820
How am I supposed to
sleep like this, you idiot?

115
00:07:13,420 --> 00:07:16,170
It is the sixth day since the
commencement of the war.

116
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:20,630
You are the first to have
made their way here.

117
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:26,469
Can I take it that you are
withdrawing from the war, boy?

118
00:07:26,470 --> 00:07:28,429
O-Of course I am!

119
00:07:28,430 --> 00:07:29,980
What else can I do, die?

120
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:35,519
Without a Servant, I can't kill
anyone, and I'm no longer a Master!

121
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:38,189
I-I'm just an ordinary human.

122
00:07:38,190 --> 00:07:39,989
If anything, I'm a victim!

123
00:07:39,990 --> 00:07:44,610
Having people come to kill me when
I can't fight back would just be unfair!

124
00:07:46,370 --> 00:07:49,240
What? Do you have
a problem with that?

125
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:51,329
Of course not.

126
00:07:51,330 --> 00:07:54,329
You are the first to
withdraw from this war...

127
00:07:54,330 --> 00:07:57,539
and the first person to use this
church's services since it was founded.

128
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:59,840
I will offer you
every hospitality.

129
00:08:00,210 --> 00:08:03,970
What? You're saying I'm the only one
who's ever been knocked out like this?

130
00:08:04,680 --> 00:08:08,260
My grandfather's gonna
kill me when he finds out!

131
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:11,979
This is all thanks
to you people!

132
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:14,600
You stuck me with that
crappy Servant, Rider!

133
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:16,060
Oh?

134
00:08:16,770 --> 00:08:19,609
Then Rider was of no use to you?

135
00:08:19,610 --> 00:08:21,029
Damn right!

136
00:08:21,030 --> 00:08:26,359
After all I did for her, she
went and died like a dog!

137
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:29,580
Any other Servant would've
been way more useful!

138
00:08:31,450 --> 00:08:34,499
Damn it, I did exactly
what Grandfather said!

139
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:36,499
My preparations were perfect!

140
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:39,709
But those bastards
got in my way!

141
00:08:39,710 --> 00:08:43,550
It was two against one! Who
can win against those odds?

142
00:08:44,130 --> 00:08:46,840
Yeah. It wasn't
my fault that I lost.

143
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:49,679
Their Servants were
better than mine! That's all!

144
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:54,519
And yet those bastards were looking
down on me with their smug expressions!

145
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:55,480
Shit!

146
00:08:55,481 --> 00:09:01,110
Shit, shit, shit, shit!

147
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:10,030
Then are you saying that you
still have the resolve to fight?

148
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:14,949
You are most fortunate.

149
00:09:14,950 --> 00:09:19,250
There happens to be
one available Servant.

150
00:09:24,550 --> 00:09:28,299
And what do you think
that doctor said to me?

151
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:31,219
"It's rare to see someone
so healthy, Fujimura-san,

152
00:09:31,220 --> 00:09:35,560
so perhaps you'd care to
donate some blood? Ho ho ho!"

153
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:39,399
I'm a patient too, damn it!

154
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:40,730
Unbelievable!

155
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:42,569
Gimme more!

156
00:09:42,570 --> 00:09:44,873
Anyway, isn't it great
news that most of

157
00:09:44,885 --> 00:09:47,489
them got away with
nothing worse than anemia?

158
00:09:47,490 --> 00:09:49,859
They didn't have to
close the school, either.

159
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:51,199
True.

160
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:54,829
I'm glad that classes
will be held as usual, but...

161
00:09:54,830 --> 00:09:56,749
It's a little strange.

162
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:58,080
Strange? How?

163
00:09:58,460 --> 00:10:00,579
Even though it was
such a big incident,

164
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:04,299
they have no idea
what really caused it.

165
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:09,049
Something about chemicals in an
empty classroom on the first floor?

166
00:10:09,050 --> 00:10:12,759
They spent all night scouring
the building from top to bottom,

167
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:14,680
and that's the only
lead they have.

168
00:10:15,140 --> 00:10:18,890
But the students in the hospital
will be able to go home soon, right?

169
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:20,940
Yeah.

170
00:10:20,941 --> 00:10:24,609
It'll differ from person to person, but
most will be able to go home today.

171
00:10:24,610 --> 00:10:26,480
Ah, Sakura-chan included.

172
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:27,899
Oh, really?

173
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:31,279
If you have time, you
should stop by and say hello.

174
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:33,950
I bet she'll be
happy to see you.

175
00:10:42,130 --> 00:10:43,590
T-Tohsaka?

176
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,670
There's definitely something
suspicious about Issei.

177
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:50,680
Suspicious? How so?

178
00:10:51,010 --> 00:10:52,549
He could be Caster's Master.

179
00:10:52,550 --> 00:10:57,099
Caster's made Ryuudou Temple her
base, and Issei comes to school from there.

180
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:59,479
Those things can't be unrelated.

181
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:02,269
Come on. It could
just be a coincidence.

182
00:11:02,270 --> 00:11:05,769
What? You're taking
Issei's side, Emiya-kun?

183
00:11:05,770 --> 00:11:08,280
It's not like that.

184
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:12,450
Come with me.

185
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:14,779
Just come on!

186
00:11:14,780 --> 00:11:15,780
Tohsaka?

187
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:21,579
Look, I get it.

188
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:24,829
I get what you're trying to say.

189
00:11:24,830 --> 00:11:27,129
So don't give me
that look, okay?

190
00:11:27,130 --> 00:11:30,299
I don't know how to handle
it when you get all sulky.

191
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:31,970
I'm not sulking!

192
00:11:32,930 --> 00:11:38,559
Either way, I can't imagine Issei working
with Caster to do those horrible things.

193
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:41,349
Have you forgotten what
Archer said yesterday?

194
00:11:41,350 --> 00:11:44,769
About Caster
controlling her Master?

195
00:11:44,770 --> 00:11:47,014
In other words, isn't
it possible that Issei

196
00:11:47,026 --> 00:11:49,230
might not even remember
that he's a Master?

197
00:11:49,690 --> 00:11:52,649
That makes sense, I guess.

198
00:11:52,650 --> 00:11:55,070
You "guess"? Do you
have a better theory?

199
00:11:55,370 --> 00:11:56,370
Well, no.

200
00:11:57,240 --> 00:12:00,330
Fine. I'll check him out.

201
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,909
Don't worry! I'll do it!

202
00:12:02,910 --> 00:12:04,329
I'll look into him.

203
00:12:04,330 --> 00:12:06,669
Leave Issei to me.

204
00:12:06,670 --> 00:12:10,050
I'll find out whether
or not he's a Master.

205
00:12:12,970 --> 00:12:14,219
Trust me.

206
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:16,969
I won't hold back just
because he's a friend.

207
00:12:16,970 --> 00:12:18,970
You know I wouldn't lie to you.

208
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:21,309
All right.

209
00:12:21,310 --> 00:12:24,850
The moment you have any idea
either way, tell me at once. Got it?

210
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:26,770
Yeah. You have my word.

211
00:12:29,610 --> 00:12:32,490
So how do you
plan to figure it out?

212
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:35,200
Um...

213
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:40,912
You aren't just going to
casually ask, "Hey, Issei,

214
00:12:40,924 --> 00:12:44,579
are you a Master?"
straight to his face, are you?

215
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:49,290
Of course not. There are ways to find
out if someone's a Master without asking.

216
00:12:54,630 --> 00:12:55,630
Emiya?

217
00:13:01,390 --> 00:13:03,019
Issei...

218
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:05,390
Don't ask questions.
Just take off your clothes.

219
00:13:07,650 --> 00:13:09,310
Wh-What did you say?

220
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:14,899
Are you mad?

221
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:18,570
Is this some new form of interrogation?
Are you gonna question me?

222
00:13:20,370 --> 00:13:22,080
That's right. And you'll answer!

223
00:13:22,450 --> 00:13:23,790
Just hurry up and strip!

224
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:29,040
Stop this, fool! You call yourself
the son of a warrior family?

225
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,710
Shut up and strip!

226
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:41,799
Oh, man. That's
a load off my mind.

227
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,809
What are you so pleased about?

228
00:13:43,810 --> 00:13:48,059
And why did you make
me strip for no reason?

229
00:13:48,060 --> 00:13:49,189
Oh, right.

230
00:13:49,190 --> 00:13:50,559
My bad, Issei.

231
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:56,400
If even you realize what you did was wrong,
then I insist that you explain this folly!

232
00:13:56,900 --> 00:14:02,159
Sorry. I can't give you the details, but
there was something I needed to make sure.

233
00:14:02,160 --> 00:14:04,660
Now that I know, we're all good.

234
00:14:11,580 --> 00:14:13,089
Say, Issei...

235
00:14:13,090 --> 00:14:16,050
Have you noticed anything
strange at the temple recently?

236
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:18,549
Strange?

237
00:14:18,550 --> 00:14:21,800
Can you think of anything
that isn't like it used to be?

238
00:14:22,550 --> 00:14:24,139
Nothing in particular.

239
00:14:24,140 --> 00:14:26,100
That mountain is the
very picture of tranquility!

240
00:14:26,470 --> 00:14:27,810
Hey, Issei!

241
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:35,649
School has now ended.

242
00:14:35,650 --> 00:14:40,150
NO ENTRY

243
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:40,150
Students are not permitted to
remain on campus after school hours.

244
00:14:40,660 --> 00:14:42,990
Please return home at once.

245
00:14:44,950 --> 00:14:45,950
She went home?

246
00:14:45,951 --> 00:14:48,910
Yes, Tohsaka-san
left a while ago.

247
00:14:49,830 --> 00:14:53,580
What the hell? She said
to report to her right away.

248
00:15:20,490 --> 00:15:21,950
Tohsaka?

249
00:15:28,290 --> 00:15:29,949
Hey, Tohsaka!

250
00:15:29,950 --> 00:15:31,620
What are you doing here...

251
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:36,380
T-T-Tohsaka, w-w-wai...

252
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:37,840
Be quiet.

253
00:15:37,841 --> 00:15:39,669
If you cause a
scene, he'll spot us.

254
00:15:39,670 --> 00:15:41,720
Who'll spot us?

255
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:44,470
Move. Stick to the wall.

256
00:15:45,260 --> 00:15:47,219
Boobs... Tohsaka, your...

257
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:48,679
I said to keep quiet.

258
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:50,559
There. In front of
Sakura's house.

259
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:52,560
See that weird
guy standing there?

260
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:58,019
Blond hair...

261
00:15:58,020 --> 00:15:59,319
A foreigner?

262
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:02,530
Right. He's been watching the
Matou house for a while now.

263
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:05,160
He's coming!

264
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:22,919
I wonder if he's the guy who
was talking to Sakura earlier.

265
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:24,300
To Sakura?

266
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:28,390
Yeah. It seemed like he was
asking Sakura for directions.

267
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:33,769
W-Wait, what are you doing here?

268
00:16:33,770 --> 00:16:36,230
I could ask you the same thing.

269
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:42,359
What's with the evil grin?

270
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:43,859
Nothing!

271
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:46,989
But that makes sense. Instead
of looking for other Masters,

272
00:16:46,990 --> 00:16:49,067
you're more concerned
about that precious junior

273
00:16:49,079 --> 00:16:50,950
of yours who always
comes over to help you.

274
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:55,119
I think I understand you a
little better now, Emiya-kun.

275
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:56,789
Don't be stupid.

276
00:16:56,790 --> 00:17:01,460
I did check out Issei, but you left
before I could tell you how it went.

277
00:17:03,170 --> 00:17:05,219
He's in the clear.

278
00:17:05,220 --> 00:17:08,179
What? You already
looked into him, Emiya-kun?

279
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:11,179
I did. Issei isn't a Master.

280
00:17:11,180 --> 00:17:13,720
Believe me or don't.

281
00:17:14,810 --> 00:17:17,479
No, I believe you.

282
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:20,269
You aren't the kind
to lie, Emiya-kun.

283
00:17:20,270 --> 00:17:23,570
If you say Issei's
innocent, then that's that.

284
00:17:25,570 --> 00:17:28,319
But how did you find out?

285
00:17:28,320 --> 00:17:31,329
I made him strip, of course.

286
00:17:31,330 --> 00:17:35,160
I had him take off his top and
checked if he had any Command Spells.

287
00:17:37,250 --> 00:17:40,000
So what are you
doing here, Tohsaka?

288
00:17:41,590 --> 00:17:44,669
I was worried about Sakura too.

289
00:17:44,670 --> 00:17:47,009
Well, we're kinda acquaintances.

290
00:17:47,010 --> 00:17:50,339
Fuji-nee said she's
being discharged today.

291
00:17:50,340 --> 00:17:52,100
She might be at home.

292
00:17:53,390 --> 00:17:54,390
Oh.

293
00:17:57,310 --> 00:17:58,770
Tohsaka? You're leaving?

294
00:18:09,070 --> 00:18:11,909
There's something
I want to ask you.

295
00:18:11,910 --> 00:18:13,910
Fine. What is it?

296
00:18:14,740 --> 00:18:17,999
Um, hypothetically...

297
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,249
How do you think someone
would feel growing up

298
00:18:21,250 --> 00:18:23,852
if they were given
away to another family

299
00:18:23,864 --> 00:18:26,670
for adoption, without
any say in the matter?

300
00:18:29,130 --> 00:18:30,220
Emiya-kun?

301
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:34,180
What kind of question is that?

302
00:18:34,890 --> 00:18:38,389
If their new home was
nice, they'd be happy,

303
00:18:38,390 --> 00:18:41,440
and if it wasn't so nice,
they'd be unhappy, right?

304
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:43,309
I see.

305
00:18:43,310 --> 00:18:44,819
Yeah, you're right.

306
00:18:44,820 --> 00:18:47,990
Why am I even asking
such an obvious question?

307
00:18:50,450 --> 00:18:54,909
Let's brainstorm ways to
find Caster at school tomorrow.

308
00:18:54,910 --> 00:18:56,950
Sure, will do.

309
00:19:07,170 --> 00:19:08,460
Ow...

310
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:14,720
It's been a while since we
practiced kendo in the dojo, Shirou.

311
00:19:15,180 --> 00:19:16,509
A while?

312
00:19:16,510 --> 00:19:19,099
Even with as fine a
sparring partner as Taiga?

313
00:19:19,100 --> 00:19:21,849
I guess it has been.

314
00:19:21,850 --> 00:19:24,479
After Dad died, I
just kind of stopped.

315
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,019
That's right.

316
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:30,650
After Kiritsugu-san died, Shirou
barely touched his bamboo sword again.

317
00:19:31,070 --> 00:19:33,109
It made me so sad.

318
00:19:33,110 --> 00:19:36,529
Don't bring up the past now.

319
00:19:36,530 --> 00:19:37,909
Hmph.

320
00:19:37,910 --> 00:19:40,789
Oh, tales from
Shirou's childhood?

321
00:19:40,790 --> 00:19:43,040
You wanna hear? Do you?

322
00:19:43,420 --> 00:19:45,539
Yes. I am curious.

323
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:50,550
All right! Then I shall
tell you everything.

324
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:54,139
He was the most
adorable little boy.

325
00:19:54,140 --> 00:20:00,060
He was so trusting of everyone,
and he'd instantly agree to any request.

326
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:03,479
But he had a strange
stubborn streak.

327
00:20:03,480 --> 00:20:07,109
Once he'd set his mind on
something, he wouldn't budge.

328
00:20:07,110 --> 00:20:10,569
I guess he was the polar opposite
of Kiritsugu-san in that regard.

329
00:20:10,570 --> 00:20:12,070
Polar opposite?

330
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:16,029
Kiritsugu-san was the kind of guy
who simply accepted everything.

331
00:20:16,030 --> 00:20:21,039
He thought good and bad were subjective.
A "what will be, will be" kind of guy.

332
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:25,459
However, if he saw someone
in need, he'd try to help.

333
00:20:25,460 --> 00:20:28,460
And Shirou would always
try to mimic Kiritsugu-san.

334
00:20:30,050 --> 00:20:32,839
His view was way more
black-and-white, though.

335
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:35,581
He'd go around and
beat up the town bullies,

336
00:20:35,593 --> 00:20:37,970
saying, "It's wrong
to do bad things!"

337
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:42,310
Yep, even back then, Shirou
was already a champion of justice.

338
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:45,939
Why a champion of justice?

339
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:48,979
That's a hard
question to answer.

340
00:20:48,980 --> 00:20:51,729
Because I look
up to it, I guess.

341
00:20:51,730 --> 00:20:53,239
You look up to it?

342
00:20:53,240 --> 00:20:55,449
To being a champion of justice?

343
00:20:55,450 --> 00:20:57,780
Yeah, I guess.

344
00:20:58,030 --> 00:21:00,029
Why is that?

345
00:21:00,030 --> 00:21:02,790
Why? Well...

346
00:21:03,660 --> 00:21:04,660
Shirou?

347
00:21:05,620 --> 00:21:07,670
Sorry. I'm gonna
head back to my room.

348
00:21:18,430 --> 00:21:22,180
What was that?
What am I afraid of?

349
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:25,180
Why a champion of justice?

350
00:21:26,690 --> 00:21:29,150
The reason I want to be
a champion of justice...

351
00:21:30,650 --> 00:21:31,480
Yeah.

352
00:21:31,481 --> 00:21:34,530
Since you couldn't
do it, I'll do it for you.

353
00:21:36,150 --> 00:21:38,989
I just wanted to
follow in his footsteps.

354
00:21:38,990 --> 00:21:42,030
Unfortunately for you,
there's no such thing.

355
00:21:42,700 --> 00:21:44,540
Let your ideals drag
you to your death.

356
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:46,659
Shut up.

357
00:21:46,660 --> 00:21:48,750
How can you know unless you try?

358
00:22:09,150 --> 00:22:15,289
We didn't understand anything

359
00:22:15,290 --> 00:22:21,459
My left hand groped for
things that vanished to my touch

360
00:22:21,460 --> 00:22:24,459
A moral conflict

361
00:22:24,460 --> 00:22:27,260
stays your hand

362
00:22:27,510 --> 00:22:30,009
and tricks you

363
00:22:30,010 --> 00:22:31,890
out of your future

364
00:22:32,140 --> 00:22:38,809
I don't know how
to protect anyone,

365
00:22:38,810 --> 00:22:44,610
and my ideals might
well be pointless,

366
00:22:44,820 --> 00:22:52,820
but I want to live my life

367
00:22:53,820 --> 00:22:58,829
The past repeats before my eyes

368
00:22:58,830 --> 00:23:06,629
Here I will trust the me
that now stands with you

369
00:23:06,630 --> 00:23:12,719
Until my dream
crumbles and withers,

370
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:18,349
I hope you will carve
out paradise with me

371
00:23:18,350 --> 00:23:22,060
Fight your fate

372
00:23:25,430 --> 00:23:27,009
We attack tonight.

373
00:23:27,010 --> 00:23:29,099
That boy isn't a winner.

374
00:23:29,100 --> 00:23:31,809
They are naught
more than sacrifices.

375
00:23:31,810 --> 00:23:34,769
Weapons... I need
weapons that will let me fight.

376
00:23:34,770 --> 00:23:36,769
You're such an irritating boy...

377
00:23:36,770 --> 00:23:38,780
Perhaps I shall kill you.

378
00:23:38,781 --> 00:23:39,780
The Fifth Contractor

379
00:23:36,820 --> 00:23:39,780
Next Time

